

    - two things suffice to conduct me to the theoretic ground of an ethic:
      the phenomenon of a cosmic safehold and our concept of moral law

               cosmic safehold  + ‘moral law’ →  ethic

        : re `cosmic safehold` see ~/work/safehold/ : *The presence throughout the cosmos
          of a safehold fit for securing our long-term survival.*
        : re `moral law` see `^*Pearsall.+2003.+Oxford dictionary of English`s @ sources.brec :
         ‘(in some systems of ethics) an absolute principle defining the criteria of right action
          (whether conceived as a divine ordinance or a truth of reason)’
        : re `ethic` see doi:10.1093/OED/2656971922 : *Oxford English dictionary*, ‘ethic (n.),
          sense b,’ June 2026. : ‘A system or set of moral principles’.
        - the first evidences a source of morals, the second represents its conduit into society,
          and the two together yield under analysis the conditions of moral law
          whose fulfillment would constitute the theoretic ground of an ethic
            : re `the first (.+ a source of morals)`
              see `^*- the phenomenon of the cosmic safehold ${same}$`
            : re `the second represents (its conduit into society)`
              see `^*- tradition gives.+that source ${same} through our concept of moral law$`
            : re `(the two).+(yield) under (analysis) (the conditions.+of an ethic)$`s
              see `^*- ${3} of ${1}.+${2}s ${4}$`p
        - the evidence shows moreover that these conditions have been met,
          thereby putting into effect an ethic of moral law
            : re `(the evidence) (shows).+(that.+)$`s see `^*- ${1}.+${2} ${3}$`p
    - the phenomenon of the cosmic safehold evidences a source of morals
        - [because] what explains the presence of that safehold?
        - an aetiologic survey that aims for exhaustive coverage by typological division
          turns up the following results


                table, Known, possible explanantia for the cosmic safehold
                    ┈

                  explain-  truth mode    name of explanans
                   able    of explanans

                    yes
                            necessary
                                          physical necessity

                                          supernatural design

                        ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                            contingent
                                          natural cosmogonal selection

                                          constrained multiverse ensemble

                                          mundane design

                    ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈
                    no
                                          null, brute fact



            : re `an aetiologic survey.+by typological division`
              see ~/work/safehold/aetiology/ : *Aetiology of the cosmic safehold.*
        - the known, possible explanantia include some artificial, some natural, and a null explanans
        - only the artificial imply a moral source
        - there are two of them

                • supernatural design by God
                    : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
                • mundane design by cosmic creators
                    : re `^*• (.+ design) .+` see `^^${same}$` @ ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec

            - both rest on what tradition gives to be such a source,
              namely a universal or cosmic creator
        - none of the three natural explanantia has any moral bearing at all
            - rather each rests on a theory of physics that has yet to be formulated,
              or a feature of nature that has yet to be discovered,
              such that the issue of what the safehold evidences and whether or not
              it bears on morals might appear to hang on future developments in physics
                : re `rests on a (theory) of (physics) that has yet to be formulated`
                  see `^*• .+structure is explainable by a.+yet unknown.+${1} of fundamental ${2}` @
                  ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
                : re `rests on a.+feature of (natur)e that has yet to be discovered`s
                  see `^*• any actual path is the cull of a.+yet unknown.+${1}al process` @
                  ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
                : re `rests on a.+feature of nature that has yet to be discovered`s
                  see `^*• the conditions.+are bound.+by a.+yet unknown.+constraint of.+cosmogony`s @
                  ~/work/safehold/aetiology/text.brec
        - but the artificial explanantia, for their part, depend on no such developments
          and need not wait on them
            - already each is determinate enough to be explicated and put to practical use
            - and as I work at that, I happen upon larger considerations that speak in favour of the
              artificial explanantia, giving me reason to believe that the safehold is indeed an artifact
              of creative design, considerations in which the presence of the safehold serves as evidence
              of that design and therewith of a source of morals in a universal or cosmic creator
                : re `(a source) of morals in (a universal or cosmic creator)`
                  see `what tradition gives to be such ${1}, namely ${2}$`p
    - tradition gives to that source its conduit into society through our concept of moral law
    - analysis of the two in conjunction (source and concept) yields the conditions of moral law
      whose fulfillment would constitute the theoretic ground of an ethic
        - the particular moral source that is evidenced determines the particular concept of moral law
        - analysis of that law’s concept yields its conditions, what it would take to realize that law
          and thereby an ethic
    - the evidence [now] shows that these conditions have been met,
      thereby putting into effect an ethic of moral law
